1) To serve as basic foundation in strengthening agrarian reform, cooperative development and other programs of the Government;

2) To cooperate and endeavor to develop capability to the eventual assumption of the operation and maintenance responsibilities of the irrigation system;

3) To serve as a channel for the government, private and international agencies in providing technical assistance and other essential services concerning irrigated agriculture and other income generating activities;

4) To sue and be sued on matters related to the operation of the Association; HCacTI

5) To enter into contracts, negotiate and secure loans from the government, non-government, private and international institutions to support the operation of the Association, its programs, projects and activities, and funds generated will be used solely by the Association;

6) To act as catalyzer for payment of loans, land amortizations, irrigation service fees, marketing of farm produce, procurement and distribution of agricultural inputs; and to facilitate similar transactions with concerned parties for the benefit and welfare of the farmers;

7) To hold, purchase and own real properties, introduce necessary improvements thereon to enhance their social and economic values and to sell, mortgage or otherwise dispose of the same as may be necessary in its operations or implementation of its programs, projects and activities;

8) To encourage participation of the farmer-irrigator's in promoting a wholesome community life;

9) To promote continuous group action/cooperative work thereby enhancing the mobilization of local resources in the implementation of the activities of the Association;

10) To implement planned thrift and savings programs among its members and initiate fund raising activities for IA capital build-up provided authorized by existing laws;

11) To conduct continuing education and training programs for IA members/officers and other members of the irrigation community;

12) To cooperate or federate with similar Associations to spearhead the growth and development process of cooperativism; and

13) To exercise all powers of a non-stock and non-profit organization under the Corporation Code of the Philippines and other existing laws.

